# deploy/*.sh are fetched with `curl | bash` onto a Raspberry Pi. A CRLF
# line ending in the shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named
# "bash\r" and the installer dies with a confusing `bad interpreter: ^M`.
# They happen to be LF in the index today only because of the current
# core.autocrlf setting; this pins it regardless of who clones the repo.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/rally-gate-net text eol=lf

# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise every file
# in the repo, which is a large and pointless diff for no benefit here.
